.TH DADHICHI 1 "2026-07-05" "dadhichi 0.1.7" "Dadhichi Manual"
.SH NAME
dadhichi \- a modern, AI-first, agent-native IDE written in Rust
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dadhichi
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ GOAL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dadhichi
boots the Dadhichi microkernel, registers the core services (AI model router,
MCP tool registry, workspace index), attaches the Agent Console to the event
bus, and drives an autonomous agent through a plan \(-> act \(-> reflect loop.
.PP
By default it runs entirely offline using a built-in mock model provider, so no
API keys or network access are required.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I GOAL
A natural-language goal for the built-in agent to plan and execute. When
omitted, a demonstration goal is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing filter (for example
.IR info " or " dadhichi=debug ).
Defaults to
.IR warn .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run the built-in demonstration:
.B dadhichi
.TP
Run the agent against your own goal:
.B dadhichi "Explain what makes Dadhichi agent-native."
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B dadhichi
exits 0 on success and non-zero if the agent run fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project home: https://github.com/pariharshyamu/Dadhichi
.SH AUTHOR
Dadhichi contributors.
